# Cloudflare Pages redirects. One rule per line: source, destination, status.
# Evaluated before static assets are served.
#
# The Contact section is part of the home page, not a page of its own. It used
# to be /contact.html, and that URL is still linked from elsewhere, so it has
# to keep resolving - but as a real 301, not as the meta-refresh stub that used
# to live here.
#
# The stub cost three hops and changed mechanism halfway through:
#
#   /contact.html -308-> /contact -200 <meta refresh>-> /index.html#contact -308-> /#contact
#
# Google follows a meta refresh as a redirect, so what it saw was a mixed
# three-hop chain, and it reported the URL as a redirect error. These two rules
# collapse that to a single permanent redirect.
#
# The fragment is for the reader, not the crawler: Google drops it and resolves
# both rules to the home page, which is the correct destination either way.
/contact.html   /#contact   301
/contact        /#contact   301
